// Each line passes straight through the package on two pads, so the array
// sits in series on the trace with no stub: IO1-A to IO1-B, IO2-A to IO2-B.
part USBLC6-2SC6 {
    @~footprint    = SOT-23-6;
    #value         = USBLC6-2SC6;
    @!type         = esd;
    #~mpn          = "USBLC6-2SC6";
    #!manufacturer = "STMicroelectronics";

    1 : IO1-A<>;
    2 : GND<   &TYPE=POWER;
    3 : IO2-A<>;
    4 : IO2-B<>;
    5 : VBUS<  &TYPE=POWER;
    6 : IO1-B<>;
};

---

# USBLC6-2SC6

**Source:** STMicroelectronics, USBLC6-2 datasheet, Doc ID 11265 Rev 5,
October 2011. SOT-23-6L package. Two-line low-capacitance ESD protection for
USB 2.0 data lines, with a diode to VBUS and a central TVS.

## Pins

| Pin | Name | Function |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | I/O1 | Line 1 |
| 2 | GND | Ground |
| 3 | I/O2 | Line 2 |
| 4 | I/O2 | Line 2, internally connected to pin 3 |
| 5 | VBUS | Supply rail clamp reference |
| 6 | I/O1 | Line 1, internally connected to pin 1 |

## Absolute maximum ratings

| Parameter | Value |
|---|---|
| Peak pulse voltage, IEC 61000-4-2 air discharge | 15 kV |
| Peak pulse voltage, IEC 61000-4-2 contact discharge | 15 kV |
| Peak pulse voltage, MIL-STD-883 human body model | 25 kV |
| Operating junction temperature | −40 to +125 °C |

## Electrical characteristics (TA = 25 °C)

| Parameter | Condition | Min | Typ | Max | Unit |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Stand-off voltage, VRM | | | | 5.25 | V |
| Breakdown voltage, VBR | IR = 1 mA | 6 | | | V |
| Leakage current | VRM = 5.25 V | | 10 | 150 | nA |
| Line capacitance, I/O to GND | VR = 1.65 V, f = 1 MHz | | 2.5 | 3.5 | pF |
| Capacitance matching, I/O to I/O | VR = 1.65 V | | | 0.04 | pF |
| Clamping voltage | IPP = 5 A, 8/20 µs | | | 17 | V |

## Application

Place the array as close to the connector as possible, with the data lines
routed through the two pads of each line so the protection adds no stub.
VBUS pin to the USB supply, GND to the ground plane with a short via.

## Package

SOT-23-6L, 2.9 × 1.6 mm body, 0.95 mm pitch. Pin 1 at the marked corner,
1–3 on one side, 4–6 on the other.
